Historical memory . L-SHADE maintains H memory slots (default H = 6 , storing location parameters (MF [k], MCR [k]) for k ∈ { 1, . . . , H }, all initialized to 0.5. When generating parameters for individual i, a memory slot Ki is sampled uniformly from {1, . . . , H }, and then:
• Fi ∼ Cauchy(MF [Ki], 0.1), regenerated if ≤ 0, truncated to 1 if > 1;
• CRi ∼ N (MCR [Ki], 0.1), clipped to [0, 1].
